; ROTATE FORTY BY FOUR  DOWNWARD  entered at the first byte of a forty byte
; run with four free cells immediately below it; every byte moves down four
; places and the first four wrap round to the top; the pointer comes back
; where it started;
;
; THIS IS THE CONVEYOR AT THE SIZE THE TEMP RUN WANTS; aes/decrypt128 stores
; ten four byte schedule temps and must write each one to a FIXED address  so
; the run turns under the write point instead of the write point moving along
; the run; An include takes no parameters  so the upward turn is a separate
; file: block/rotate40up4;
;
; MEASURED AT 122 THOUSAND 524 INSTRUCTIONS A TURN on random bytes  against
; the 138 million of one decrypted block; Nineteen turns  ten storing and
; nine reading  come to 2 million 328 thousand: one point seven percent; The
; alternative was turning the whole 176 byte schedule at 1 million 300
; thousand a turn  and HANDOFF carries both measurements;
; every byte moves down four places  the lowest four into the scratch
